    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0656" n="644" xml:id="pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/31644: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-13T13:30:00-03:00">October 13, 1943—1:30
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 20—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–2321. My telegram 4760, October 8, 11:00 a.m.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d590-f1"/>
                    General Dutra says that he understands that no definite plans can be made
                    without the approval of the Combined Chiefs of Staff. However, he says, Brazil
                    is making all preparations and will be ready to send the first division in
                    December.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
